title: Rosacea
---

# Rosacea

- **Definition** - chronic inflammatory condition affecting the central face, which is distinct from acne vulgaris, where sebum excretion is normal and comedones are absent
- **Clinical features of rosacea** - exacerbated by heat, sunlight and alcohol:
  - **Heterogenous skin manifestations:**
    - Intermittent flushing followed by fixed erythema and telangiectasiae
    - Papules and pustules
    - Rhinophyma (soft-tissue overgrowth of the nose)
    - Facial lymphoedema
  - **Eye involvement** - conjunctivitis and blepharitis
- **Mx:**
  - **Principles of Mx:**
    - <u>Topical therapy</u> - e.g. topical antimicrobials (e.g. azelaic acid, metronidazole)
    - <u>Systemic therapy</u> - e.g. ABx (tetracycline, erythromycin), isoretinoin
